; Regression test for issue #3281: with --pivot, the pivoted copy of a
; declared account was itself treated as declared.
;
; --pivot moves each posting onto a temporary account such as
; `Fund:Vanguard:Equity:Opening balance` before --limit filters it, and that
; account inherited the flags of the original -- including the mark left by
; the `account` directive.  When --limit then rejected every posting of a
; declared account, --empty and the accounts listing still showed its
; pivoted copy, an account that no posting in the report uses.  The
; declared accounts themselves are still listed under their own names.

account Assets:Pension
account Equity:Opening balance

2022-01-01 * Opening
    ; Fund: Vanguard
    Assets:Pension             100.00 GBP
    Equity:Opening balance

2022-01-11 Monthly fee
    ; Fund: Vanguard
    Expenses:Fees                5.00 GBP
    Assets:Pension

; Only the fee is uncleared, so the opening balance must not appear under
; Fund:Vanguard.
test --empty bal --pivot Fund --uncleared
                   0  Assets:Pension
                   0  Equity:Opening balance
                   0  Fund:Vanguard
           -5.00 GBP    Assets:Pension
            5.00 GBP    Expenses:Fees
--------------------
                   0
end test

test accounts --pivot Fund --uncleared
Assets:Pension
Equity:Opening balance
Fund:Vanguard:Assets:Pension
Fund:Vanguard:Expenses:Fees
end test

; The second command from the issue report, on data tagged with the fund:
; every posting is rejected, so nothing appears under Fund:Vanguard.
test --empty bal --pivot Fund -l 'commodity !~ /GBP/'
                   0  Assets:Pension
                   0  Equity:Opening balance
--------------------
                   0
end test
